#X text 240 83 || Versions <5.0;
#X text 240 108 The BCM283x SoC supports 2 hardware PWM channels. By
default \, the channels are mapped as follows:;
#X text 240 148 • PWM0 = GPIO12/GPIO18;
#X text 240 173 • PWM1 = GPIO13/GPIO19;
#X text 240 198 Consult the official documentation on how to enable
and configure these.;
#X text 240 238 Note: the Raspberry Pi?s analog audio output uses both
PWM channels. Playing audio and simultaneously accessing a PWM channel
may cause issues.;
#X text 240 293 ~;
#X text 240 318 || Raspberry Pi 5 and later;
#X text 240 343 The Raspberry Pi 5 support 4 hardware PWM channels.
By default \, the channels are mapped as follows:;
#X text 240 383 • PWM0 = GPIO12;
#X text 240 408 • PWM1 = GPIO13;
#X text 240 433 • PWM2 = GPIO18;
#X text 240 458 • PWM3 = GPIO19;
#X text 240 483 Consult the official documentation on how to enable
and configure these.;
#X text 240 523 ~;
#X text 240 548 Some of the GPIO pins capable of supporting hardware
PWM can also be configured for use with other peripherals. Be careful
not to enable two peripherals on the same pin at the same time.;
